# Copy to .env and fill in to enable a real Google Sheets connection.
# Without these, "Connect Google Sheet" falls back to the mock deals.
#
# Google Cloud Console setup:
#   1. Create a project, enable the "Google Sheets API".
#   2. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application) and add this app's
#      origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173) under Authorized JavaScript origins.
#   3. Create an API key and restrict it to HTTP referrers + the Sheets API —
#      it ships inside the client bundle, so treat it as public, not secret.
#   4. Share the target spreadsheet with the Google account you'll sign in
#      with, and lay out a sheet named "Inputs" with labels in column A and
#      values in column B (see src/mocks/sample-deal.xlsx for the layout).
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
VITE_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_SHEET_RANGE=Inputs!A1:B12
